  "notes": "Single-storey charcoal-painted stucco front with full-height vertical-slat steel gates across most of it and one steel door. A grey panel front with a roll-up (t 0-0.2) and a brown timber front with boarded doors (0.2-0.4) west of the charcoal front; the charcoal part has two 3 m slat gates and a black door instead of three full-height gates. A gridded window behind a grille where the first slat gate was; the brown front gets a framed shop window instead of a flat boarded plane. Darker weathered brown timber front. Street grime: soot at the base, grime, faint wide streaks. Charcoal awninged bay (dark), dark vertical-board timber with a projecting dark box window, black stucco with three vertical-bar grilles; the west panel is charcoal not brown; the glazed openings on the black part became grilles. The boarded timber doors are closed and opaque, not a see-through opening. Charcoal (grey, not brown) stucco, weathered mid-brown plank wood, box bay in charcoal-grey with a gridded window, small dark steel door.",
